Subject: SUMMARY: Correct Sendmail Permissions
X-MARC-Message: https://marc.info/?l=tru64-unix-managers&m=96078615810699

Hi Everyone,

I knew I could count on this list!

Correct permissions for Berkeley sendmail 8.8.6 can be set as I thought:
chmod 4755.  It is not necessary to restart Sendmail after the permissions
have been changed.

Jim Lochowitz also suggested that I use 4555, since root doesn't need write
permissions.  This made perfect sense to me, so this is what I went with.

Big thanks to the following for responding so quickly!

Amy E. Skowronek" <amy@aloha.nascom.nasa.gov
Jim Lochowitz <jlochowi@cs.ucsd.edu>
Paul A Sand <pas@unh.edu>
John T." <johnt@net.bluemoon.net>
Mervyn Weis <WeisM@mail.dec.com>

and all the others who may be sending mail while I'm posting my summary.

