From tru64-unix-managers  Tue Aug 26 14:04:42 1997
From: "Tim Couger" <Tim.Couger () MCI ! Com>
Date: Tue, 26 Aug 1997 14:04:42 +0000
To: tru64-unix-managers
Subject: SUMMARY: Configuring a Network Printer Under DU4.0b
X-MARC-Message: https://marc.info/?l=tru64-unix-managers&m=96078615810608

Right after I sent the note, I kicked myself for not searching the
archives first (where I could've found the answer).  The URL for Dwight
Walker's summary on configuring network printers is:

http://www.ornl.gov/its/archives/mailing-lists/alpha-osf-managers/1997/05/msg00581.html

I did receive all sorts of replies.  Since I don't have access to the NT
server that hosts the printer, I pursued modifying the /etc/printcap
config file.  From all the responses, I gleaned the following config:

#-------
tlcraw|raw printer:\
        :lp=:\
        :sd=/usr/spool/lpd/tlcraw:\
        :rm=printerIP:\
        :rp=raw:
tlctext|text printer:\
        :lp=:\
        :sd=/usr/spool/lpd/tlctext:\
        :rm=printerIP:\
        :rp=text:
#-------

Plain text files get sent to 'tlctext' and postscript files get sent to
'tlcraw' (the printer will autoswitch between PCL and PostScript).

Thanks to all who replied ... Yizhong Zhou, Robert L. McMillin, Craig I.
Hagan, Tim Winders, Ray Stell, Alex Nord, Jason Bingham, Gary C.
Jenkins, Joe Spanicek, and Dwight Walker.

