From tru64-unix-managers  Thu Aug 21 13:22:07 1997
From: "Johan M Erlank" <j_erlank () sames ! co ! za>
Date: Thu, 21 Aug 1997 13:22:07 +0000
To: tru64-unix-managers
Subject: vdump/vrestore: summary
X-MARC-Message: https://marc.info/?l=tru64-unix-managers&m=96078615810539

Thanx for all the answers I received. All of them were really 
helpful, and I'm on my way now. A brief summary:

I was told that instead of using rmt0h, I should use nrmt0h, the 
non-rewind device. also, if a fileset is not mounted, eg. /cdrom, it 
will not be backed up. To limit problems, umount /proc and remount it 
afterwards. mt -f /dev/nrmt0h fsf n will skip to the necessary 
saveset on the tape, from which I then use vrestore -f /dev/nrmt0h -i 
to interactively restore the data. 

Only problem is to fit 6 gigs' compressed data on a 4 gig tape ;)

Rgds,

Johan Erlank

