Subject: [SUMMARY] Runaway Xdec?
X-MARC-Message: https://marc.info/?l=tru64-unix-managers&m=96078615810514

Hi DU Admins

I got two quick replies to my question about a runaway Xdec
process and a blank console monitor on a 433au running DU4.0c.

Thanks to Robert L. McMillin and Karim Keshavjee.  Karim's reply
provided the solution.  This is a known bug affecting systems
with the 4D40T graphics card.  There is a patch for this in
the latest DU4.0C patch kit.

The problem appears at regular times including:

   Mon Aug 18 00:26:01 1997
   Mon Oct  6 17:28:48 1997

I had to use 'kill -KILL' to kill the process.  Then I did
'/sbin/init.d/xlogin stop' followed by '.. start'.
Now everything is working fine and I can log in at the console 
again.


Thanks
Ian

