To: tru64-unix-managers
Subject: [SUMMARY] Disklabel weirdness.
X-MARC-Message: https://marc.info/?l=tru64-unix-managers&m=96078615810481

Hi DU Admins

I only received one reply to my question about anomalous arithmetic
in a disk label for an rz29b under DU 4.0B.  That was from Mike at
obrien@splusnet.com who reported the same problem under DU 3.2G 
but he thinks only after he installed some patches.

My tentative conclusion is that this is a bug in the unpatched
DU4.0B disklabel and in some patched 3.2x versions.

I also got one reply to my second question about anomalous
arithmetic in a disklabel for an RZ1BB-BS with dynamic geometry.
That was from John Holden and this is his answer:

> 	I think that you are seeing and interaction of two things :-
> 
> 1)	High density disk drives use zone recording methods. This means 
> 	that there are more sectors per track on outer tracks than on inner-
> 	tracks. There is no scope in disktab to reflect this properly, so
> 	that the sectors/cylinder is an approximation to allow some
> 	reasonable guesses for disk layout and cylinder groups.
> 
> 2)	The  sectors/unit value (partition c) is actually read directly from
> 	the disk using a SCSI 'inquiry' command and reflects the actual
> 	number of blocks available. You could lie about the disk type
> 	when you create the disk label, but the value for partition c will
> 	still be correct.


Thanks
Ian

