Hi everybody.

This is the announcement for a small new package named TapeUtils which 
includes some tools to improve and simplify tapes handling on Digital
Unix.

TapeUtils includes a VMS-like tape units allocation/deallocation system and 
an enhanced version of Ed Bailey's popular juke-box loader control program,
which supports both the allocation/deallocation system and a by-user
access permission control. The tools were developed to satisfy some
site-specific needs, but maybe they are useful for someone else.

More information can be found at the TapeUtils home page 
http://www.ts.infn.it/computing/TapeUtils/. The kit is available through
anonymous FTP at  ftp://ftp.ts.infn.it/pub/unix/TapeUtils/.

Greetings,
	
